-# locals: (sources:)
-# One compact chip per source: its name and when it was fresh. The table it
-# came from and the snapshot id are for whoever is debugging, so they sit in
-# the tooltip. A source never loaded says so, and Demand says what that leaves
-# out. No retry: the loads run in the ETL, not from here.
%ul.sources{ "aria-label": "Data sources" }
  %li.sources-label Data sources
  - sources.each do |type, snapshot|
    - if snapshot
      %li.source.live.freshness{ title: "#{snapshot.source_file} · snapshot ##{snapshot.id}" }
        %span.dot>
        %strong= t("sources.#{type}")
        = snapshot.fresh_as_of&.strftime("%b %d, %H:%M") || "—"
    - elsif type == "demand"
      %li.source.not-loaded.impact
        %span.dot>
        %strong= t("sources.#{type}")
        not loaded — forecast coverage unavailable
    - else
      %li.source.not-loaded
        %span.dot>
        %strong= t("sources.#{type}")
        not loaded
